      "message": "I\u0027ve had a look at `GrubBootControl.cpp` and thought it seemed it was designed to be compatible with single slot systems too. There\u0027s an empty slot fallback included `if (current_slot.empty()) current_slot \u003d mSlots.front();` which appeared to be there to explicitly support A-only devices. Additionally, there\u0027s a dedicated `getNumberSlots()`/`mSlots.size()` method and `IsValidSlot(slot)` guards already. This made me believe that it was intended to support single slot builds too.\n\nTesting shows the HAL works correctly on non-A/B builds bar that specific problematic line. At first glance that line seemed like a UB bug regardless, so I figured I should just patch it. Context of all this was I was getting boot failures with `AB_OTA_UPDATER\u003dfalse` on `virtio_*` targets. I guess I could potentially patch it downstream but this seems to be the cleanest approach.",
